+    Prefer the exact SQLSTATE, but fall back to the SQLAlchemy exception type so a
+    real deadlock/FK still retries even if SQLSTATE extraction misses (the asyncpg
+    wrapping chain varies). On a domain DELETE the only possible IntegrityError is
+    the send_logs FK, and OperationalError covers deadlock/lock-timeout/
+    serialization/statement-timeout — all safe to re-run since the work is
+    idempotent.
+    """
+    if _sqlstate(exc) in _RETRYABLE_SQLSTATES:
+        return True
+    return isinstance(exc, (IntegrityError, OperationalError))
